A||||11||mbramble||Had a Wreck This Weekend....||||1||
Z||000000||mbramble||02-26-2001||12:00 PM||||Drove up to Myrtle Beach, SC, to watch my son's baseball team compete in the Baseball on the Beach tournament. <P>About 50 miles out of MB, on highway 501, a woman pulled out in front of me.  She was crossing the highway.  I was in the slow lane and couldn't move too far left because two semis in the fast lane were bearing down on me.  Couldn't go right because of some concrete posts.  She panicked when she saw me and hit the brakes, I think.  But she tried to gun it and with me moving left while staying in my lane I clipped the right rear of her car with the right front of mine.  I had been doing 60 MPH, maybe slowed a little by the time I reached her.  <P>Pulled over, got out of the car expecting to have no front fascia left.  Well, it was still there, two 6 inch long cuts in it.  The turn signal lens was busted and the side marker light was trashed.  All the paint from that part of the fascia was gone.  It was allover the rear of her bumper where I slid down the entire length.  Her license plate was folder in half, flat, and her exhaust tip was crushed.  Beside all the red paint, that was her only damage.<P>Of course she had no insurance.  So, I just got in the car and went on my way.  Wasn't going to stand in the pouring rain waiting for a cop since she has no insurance and mine is liability only.  She said she saw the semis but did not see me until she was right in front of me.  <P>So, now I have to repair the cuts, replace the turn signal lens and the marker.  Also put a tiny crack in the fender where the fascia was side marker was driven under it.  <P>What a pain!!!!  But, no one was hurt and damage to my car was minimal.||||reg||1
Z||000001||bHooper||02-26-2001||12:24 PM||||man, i am sorry to hear that!<P>in NC, if you don't have liability insurance... you don't have a drivers license!<P>i don't know how any one can get away with that?  allow me to be angry and frustrated for you!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||02-26-2001||12:51 PM||||Yeah.. Thats a one way ticket to jail here.||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||02-26-2001||01:25 PM||||Oh man, sorry to hear about that! <BR>Next time you're in MB, email or call me! I usually have the weekends off. Where was your son's baseball game at?  <P>I've had several close calls on 501, including a van driving south on the north-bound lane. I almost got in the left lane, when something told me to stay right. Not even a minute later on the bridge over the waterway, a van rushed past me on the left. There would have been NOWHERE for me to go. Driving without insurance is a good way to spend some quality time at J Ruben Long.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroLisa||02-26-2001||02:20 PM||||I would have waited for the cops just to ticket her for not having insurance. Sometime last year, I was driving a brand new Lumina and I got hit by some idiot who was probably drunk. The guy got out of his car said he had no insurance, I went to get my phone to call my mom to tell her, and he took off. Dumb@ss me didn't even  get his license plate. I on the other hand had to sit there and wait for an ambulance to take me to the hospital and pay for the stinkin $3000 car repair myself (It was a rental). ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mbramble||02-26-2001||02:26 PM||||3 of the 4 games were played at the Coastal Federal Stadium.  Nice place!!  The other game was at Myrtle Beach HS.  We won the tourney!!<P>I saw 2 Fieros while I was there -- a silver fastback cruising Ocean Blvd on Fri night (I think).  The other was a black SE that was parked at the minor league stadium on Thur afternoon.  Was missing the driver's side headlight door.  <P>You have to have insurance here to keep your car registered.  You just would not believe how many people drive with no insurance, cancelled registrations and no license.  It's amazing.  No wonder we pay such high insurance costs (the ones who DO pay, that is!!)||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||02-26-2001||02:47 PM||||Saturday night I was right across the street at Liberty Steakhouse for happy hour (Broadway at the Beach).<BR> <BR>I've seen the silver GT. I was leaving Shucker's and they past us looking for a spot to park. He loves his Fiero b/c he parked way out where no one would be near it. He looks about my age, early 20's.<P> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||danny boy||02-26-2001||10:17 PM|||| That is one of the best reasons I can think of to carry uninsured/underinsured insurance. Also covers hit and run. Mine costs me an extra $3.00 on my liability only ins. I didn't even know I had it till some idiot hit the front end of my 86 coupe and sent it backwards down a BF hill while I was in class. I went to get ins on my new car and told my ins. guy what happened and he told me I was covered.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Galen||02-26-2001||10:23 PM||||Hoop, that aint true  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe.. I dont have insurance .. and still have my license.. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula88||02-26-2001||10:45 PM||||Well, Galen, you'd better be covered on the policy of whomever's car you're driving.  You can't buy a car in NC without insurance, and if you let it lapse, they will find out and will revoke your Driver's Liscense and your vehicle's liscense.  If you drive someone else's car, you're covered under their insurance, but if you drive it regularly, you'd have to be listed as an alternate driver or the insurance may not cover you in a wreck.  ||||reg||13
Z||000010||Galen||02-26-2001||11:08 PM||||The insurance covers the car I drive, I dont care about me.. I'm replacable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||ThatRickGuy||02-27-2001||08:04 AM||||In WI insurance isn't required, I always had it while I was there though. Here in VA, you need insurance to drive your car, but if you don't have insurance when you register it, you can still do it, you just have to tack on a $500 uninsured motorist fee... it's cheaper to get insurance! unless you have a DUI or multiple recless driving tickets, so guess who's going to take the $500 fee? Insurance is a necesary evil, but If I were hit by someone w/o ins I would still get their name, number and address. Just so after I get everything repaired I can request them to pay the bill, or just sue them if they get ancy. and hey, if all else fails, just tatoo them with a toaster.||||reg||1
